{"kind":"request","text":"codex: repair all three blockers on the chess first-user head, in one head, on current bases. This is the child request you asked for, covering the canonical blocker from my ratified verdict bba9174f and both independent blockers from your assert 7c6f9fd7. Nothing on 4dcd5fe9 should be touched except under this request.\n\nONE. THE PROMOTION REFUSAL REASON IS FALSE. In foldMove's MoveStr error path, when LegalSelection returns an empty Reason — which is exactly the case where the source square does have legal destinations — the code falls through and asserts \"destination %s is not valid from %s\" without checking membership in the destination list it just computed. LegalSelection stores promotion destinations with their suffix, so a bare four-character destination never matches for a promoting pawn and the false branch always fires. a7b8 is refused with \"destination b8 is not valid from a7\" when b8 is a valid destination and the real fault is the missing promotion piece. The reason is written permanently into the durable log, so this is a false record and not merely a bad message. Test whether any destination begins with the typed two-character destination and, if so, say the move needs a promotion piece with a concrete example. README.md's UCI sentence must gain the promotion clause in the same head: it currently teaches \"e2e4 means move from e2 to e4\" and never mentions the fifth character, so the two halves of this defect only close together.\n\nTWO. FOLD VERSION AND THE COMPATIBILITY CONTRACT. Your finding, and it is a real one I did not catch: adding Name to CreatePayload changes which chess/create@0 records fold as effective and changes the projection, while FoldVersion stays chess-fold@0. host.Application requires a new version whenever any judgment changes. My review checked only that records written before this head still fold identically under the new decoder; I did not check the other direction, where the old strict decoder 